1
00:01:30,566 --> 00:01:31,551
=Tigers Sniff the Rose=

2
00:01:31,551 --> 00:01:33,560
(Based on the novel of the same name by Yiren Kuikui)

3
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,900
=Episode 2=

4
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:39,860
(Santu County Office)
Get out!

5
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,860
(Santu County Office)

6
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:53,660
Go!

7
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,980
(Merit Through the Ages)

8
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:01,780
(It's him.)

9
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,580
(He's actually still alive.)

10
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,860
(Merit Through the Ages)

11
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:10,620
May I ask, sir,

12
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,340
what was the name
of the military officer

13
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:14,660
who just rode by?

14
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,940
What's it to you?

15
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,260
Why are you asking?

16
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,180
When I saw him just now,

17
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,340
I thought

18
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,140
I recognized
an old acquaintance of mine.

19
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:23,620
An old acquaintance?

20
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:27,100
Captain Zhang received transfer orders.

21
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:29,420
He's been promoted and is passing
through here on his way to the capital.

22
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,140
How could he be
an old acquaintance of yours?

23
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:33,740
Captain Zhang?

24
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:36,060
His surname is Zhang?

25
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:37,340
You must've mistaken him.

26
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,500
The last time I saw him,

27
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,980
he was still in the Shence Army.

28
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:44,300
I never imagined

29
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:45,660
that now,

30
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:48,300
he'd have such a bright future.

31
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:56,980
Sanlang!

32
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:58,820
Dalang, Shang, run!

33
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:01,860
Father!

34
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:08,260
(Xie Jinghui, Yan Shang's Mother)

35
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,260
Jinghui!

36
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:10,780
Mother!

37
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,220
(Young Yan Shang)

38
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,820
(Come have a look!)

39
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,260
(Candied hawthorns!)

40
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,380
(Come and see!)

41
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,500
(Tasty and affordable!)

42
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:30,580
(Top quality! Take a look!)

43
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,780
(Meat)
(Come have a look!)

44
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:37,300
(Finely crafted, sturdy and durable!)

45
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:37,820
(Take care.)

46
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,140
(Come have a look!)

47
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:42,500
(Everything's freshly made!)

48
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:43,940
(Promoted to a post in the capital...)

49
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,140
(So, he's going to Sheng'an.)

50
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,740
(Sheng'an...)

51
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,900
(Shuying Rouge House)
(Ladies, feel free to browse here too.)

52
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,140
(Come have a look!)

53
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:58,700
This is the most fashionable shade.

54
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:01,020
Don't apply it all over.
Just dab it on that spot.

55
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,660
What brings a man here?

56
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,060
Don't bother looking.

57
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:05,780
He's obviously here to buy makeup.

58
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:07,140
He must already have a wife.

59
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:10,380
How come other women's husbands
know what to buy?

60
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:11,780
Sir,

61
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:13,260
what can I get for you?

62
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,740
Are these all the rouge shades

63
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:16,780
you have?

64
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:31,140
You're quite a picky young man.

65
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,100
(Sappan Rouge)
All our shades in storage are here.

66
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:34,100
You won't find

67
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,620
a wider range of shades anywhere else.

68
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,100
I want this one.

69
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:57,740
Sir, don't mind me saying so,

70
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,140
but this shade isn't very fashionable.

71
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,500
It sold well a few years ago.

72
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,020
But nowadays...

73
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:10,620
Here.

74
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:12,060
Oh...

75
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:16,540
A box of rouge doesn't cost this much.

76
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:17,980
I'm not buying this box of rouge.

77
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:19,380
I just want to know

78
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,060
how rouge in this shade

79
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,420
is made.

80
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,780
Well...

81
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,100
Sir,

82
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:28,140
don't underestimate women's cosmetics.

83
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,780
They're quite complicated to make.

84
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:31,140
The techniques
are hard to learn and remember.

85
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,140
Just teach me, miss.

86
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,180
I'll remember

87
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,220
and learn how to make it.

88
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:36,820
Well...

89
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:51,700
Are you resting, my lady?

90
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:53,180
What is it?

91
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:56,660
I've come to apologize to you.

92
00:05:59,340 --> 00:05:59,860
Come in.

93
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:12,140
You really know
when to swallow your pride.

94
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,700
I slapped you this morning,

95
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,380
and by tonight, you're over it?

96
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:18,780
Not over it.

97
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,060
I understand now.

98
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,580
That rouge must've meant a lot to you.

99
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,540
I can't truly understand how you feel.

100
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:27,540
This morning,

101
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,460
you weren't just angry.

102
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:30,900
You were hurt, too.

103
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:33,740
Why are you telling me all this?

104
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,620
Want another slap?

105
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:47,220
What's this?

106
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:49,100
Tools for making rouge.

107
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,060
I remember the shade of that rouge.

108
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:52,860
It was the color of crimson clouds.

109
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:54,460
I want to try making some

110
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:55,860
and make you a new box of rouge.

111
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:01,180
You know how to make rouge?

112
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:24,840
♪The midsummer breeze
blows soft and sweet♪

113
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:29,140
♪Fireflies dance freely
through the night♪

114
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:32,980
♪Chasing the beauty
of this fleeting world♪

115
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:37,500
♪A thousand lights turn night into day♪

116
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:41,440
♪Cicada songs mingle with the wine♪

117
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:45,900
♪Their songs linger
through the passing years♪

118
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:50,320
♪Life is but a fleeting stay♪

119
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:54,100
♪How lucky I am to walk this path
with you♪

120
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:59,040
♪Playing out life's game,
forever by your side♪

121
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:02,980
♪Innocent through the years♪

122
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:06,980
♪I thought time might stand still♪

123
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:10,860
♪Forever at that crossroads♪

124
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:15,620
♪Watching flowers bloom and fade♪

125
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:19,700
♪Weathering life's rise and fall♪

126
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:24,300
♪Turns out, unspoken tenderness♪

127
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:28,540
♪Is starlight caught in your eyes♪

128
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:34,100
Is it right?

129
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:35,060
It's close.

130
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,220
Very close.

131
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:05,540
No, that's not right.

132
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,740
The shade is a little too light.

133
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:09,860
No.

134
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,820
When it was freshly made,

135
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:16,180
it was exactly this color.

136
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:23,020
The rouge that was destroyed

137
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,500
was made by my mother

138
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,620
with her own hands.

139
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:32,940
It was the only keepsake

140
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:35,780
she left me.

141
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:47,180
Yan Shang,

142
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:48,540
thank you.

143
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:50,940
How can I ever thank you?

144
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,180
Don't rush to answer.

145
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,100
Give it some thought.

146
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:21,620
What happened

147
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,220
to your face?

148
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,260
A branch scratched me.

149
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:29,740
No.

150
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:31,580
It's a whip mark.

151
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:34,140
Again, you're not telling me the truth.

152
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:40,700
I ran into someone

153
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:42,220
on the road today.

154
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,700
He whipped me once.

155
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:52,300
Does it still hurt?

156
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:18,140
It's late.

157
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:20,460
My lady,

158
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,020
you should get some rest.

159
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:42,980
You're finally back, huh?

160
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,300
Why are you still awake, Father?

161
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,500
You're still awake too, aren't you?

162
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:53,460
Busy making rouge for that woman.

163
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,940
You grew up steeped in books,

164
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:40,220
yet you fawn over that woman.

165
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,740
Have you no shame?

166
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:50,860
Yes.

167
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:53,420
I am fawning over her.

168
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:57,020
You...

169
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:00,220
Have you no shame?

170
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:04,420
Father,

171
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:06,820
I want to leave here

172
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,300
and go to Sheng'an.

173
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:09,900
She's an honored guest from Sheng'an.

174
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,100
She can give me that opportunity.

175
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,980
You're nothing but a country bumpkin.

176
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:37,900
You think you'll make a name
for yourself in Sheng'an?

177
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,460
You think groveling at her feet

178
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:42,700
will send you soaring through the ranks?

179
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,060
It's better than doing nothing.

180
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,220
Better than
pretending to live in seclusion

181
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:54,140
when you're really just running away.

182
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,700
Better than living like you,

183
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:58,500
hiding in this wretched backwater
your whole life,

184
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,940
shutting out the world like a coward!

185
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:09,060
Get out!

186
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:10,460
Father,

187
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:12,060
don't be angry.

188
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:13,340
Shang isn't like that.

189
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:13,780
Silence!

190
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,140
Want to get out with him too?

191
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,020
Shang...

192
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:27,300
Brother.

193
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:30,500
What's wrong?

194
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:41,740
Thank you.

195
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:47,220
Brother, why do you suddenly
want to go to Sheng'an?

196
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:48,740
It's not like you.

197
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:52,700
What am I like, then?

198
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:55,780
You're clever

199
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:57,380
but stubborn to a fault.

200
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:58,860
You're even-tempered,

201
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,100
yet you worry too much.

202
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,500
You seem to want nothing,

203
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:03,900
yet something weighs on your mind.

204
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:07,100
And I don't know what it is.

205
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:10,620
Xiaozhou,

206
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:12,380
if one day

207
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:13,860
I leave Lingnan,

208
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,980
the whole family
will be counting on you.

209
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:16,940
You're leaving?

210
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,700
If anyone comes
looking for the lady later,

211
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:22,460
whatever they ask,

212
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:23,420
just say you don't know.

213
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:25,580
All right.

214
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:26,700
I understand.

215
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,500
The officers have been searching

216
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,940
all over the hills since early morning.

217
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:35,700
They'll probably find this place soon.

218
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:36,700
Your Highness,

219
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,260
something about this doesn't add up.

220
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:39,700
Lingnan is full of hills and forests.

221
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:41,100
We've already hidden ourselves here.

222
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:42,260
How did they find us again?

223
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,980
Those men are like flies.

224
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:46,420
You can't get rid of them.

225
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:47,260
Shall we see them?

226
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:48,260
No.

227
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:48,820
All right.

228
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:49,980
I'll move the carriage.

229
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:57,900
Your Honor,

230
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:58,460
over there!

231
00:16:58,900 --> 00:16:59,740
There's a house over there, too!

232
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:01,820
Careful.

233
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:11,140
Anyone home?

234
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,020
I'm Zheng Chengqing,
magistrate of Santu County.

235
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:21,540
Sorry to intrude.

236
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:32,060
Young man,

237
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,580
is there an honored guest staying here?

238
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:35,780
Yes.

239
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:38,260
But the lady left this morning.

240
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:39,540
If you don't believe me,

241
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,940
check the carriage tracks at my door.

242
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:48,060
Your Honor!

243
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:48,900
There...

244
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:50,260
there are carriage tracks!

245
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,700
After crossing all these hills,

246
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:58,620
we finally found this place,

247
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:00,380
only to be one step too late.

248
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:08,620
Your Honor, have some water.

249
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:09,820
No, no.

250
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:11,460
Chengqing!

251
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,700
Chengqing.

252
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,300
Careful.

253
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:31,980
Yan Zhanzhi!

254
00:18:32,260 --> 00:18:34,300
Chengqing, after decades apart,

255
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,540
I never imagined

256
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:37,220
we'd live to meet again.

257
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,020
Zhanzhi,

258
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:48,580
I never thought we'd meet again either.

259
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:51,900
Back then, you were renowned
throughout the capital.

260
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:55,260
Your talent far surpassed ours.

261
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:57,420
(So his father)

262
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:00,260
(is Yan Zhanzhi,
the famous scholar of his day.)

263
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:03,300
(Back then, he placed third
in the palace exam,)

264
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:05,060
(and married a noble lady
of the Xie family.)

265
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:06,540
(Now...)

266
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:08,300
(he's ended up in Lingnan.)

267
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:09,740
To be frank,

268
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,940
my son is now registered
in the Capital Prefecture

269
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:14,740
and is preparing for the imperial exams.

270
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:16,300
Look at your sons.

271
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,180
They've become nothing
but country bumpkins!

272
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:21,540
Then again,

273
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:23,980
your whole family ended up here,

274
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,060
without household registration
all these years, right?

275
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,940
So you can't sit for the imperial exams.

276
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:30,060
Father.

277
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:31,140
Father.

278
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:32,220
- How did I not notice?
- Easy.

279
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:33,420
You're paralyzed!

280
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,020
You're not even whole anymore.

281
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,740
You smug little upstart!

282
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:39,900
Chengqing!

283
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:40,620
Brother.

284
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:41,700
- You...
- Take Father back to his room to rest.

285
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:42,140
- All right.
- Father!

286
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:42,780
I'll see to Uncle Zheng.

287
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:43,140
Father!

288
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:44,100
Shang!

289
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:44,860
Xiaozhou, go back, too.

290
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:46,180
- What a hypocrite!
- Father!

291
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:46,540
Steady now.

292
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,340
You contemptible wretch,

293
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,060
always currying favor with the powerful!

294
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:49,740
Enough, Father.

295
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:50,820
You hypocrite!

296
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:51,540
Say no more.

297
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,300
You hypocrite!

298
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:58,580
You'll meet a bad end!

299
00:19:58,820 --> 00:19:59,620
Uncle, I'm sorry about that.

300
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:04,060
You're over fifty now, aren't you?

301
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:06,580
And you've become a county magistrate.

302
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,980
They say success comes to the young.

303
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:09,980
But I don't think so.

304
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,740
Take you, for example.
You're no longer young,

305
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:13,900
yet you've finally found success.

306
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,620
Shouldn't we congratulate you?

307
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:17,980
Congratulations!

308
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,300
Who do you think you are?

309
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:26,260
A family of unregistered vagrants!

310
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:28,700
Uncle, you're right.

311
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,540
We're indeed wanderers

312
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:31,780
under no one's jurisdiction.

313
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,300
But you're an official now,

314
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,220
subject to the court's
annual evaluations.

315
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:39,980
You'd best not associate with us

316
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:40,820
country bumpkins.

317
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:43,380
Wouldn't want to tarnish
your reputation as an official.

318
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:51,100
Safe travels, Uncle.

319
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,740
Wait, what are you up to?

320
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,260
You swore up and down
and brought us here.

321
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:58,300
How dare you make a fool of me?

322
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:01,700
Sir,

323
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:04,180
your magistrate is long gone.

324
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:15,780
So you led them here?

325
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:49,420
So,

326
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:51,780
you know who I am.

327
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:54,140
I was only guessing.

328
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:57,700
You're that scared of me?

329
00:21:58,660 --> 00:21:59,620
That sick of me?

330
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:02,300
So afraid I'll stay one more day

331
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:04,860
that you're racking your brains
to get rid of me?

332
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:05,940
Yan Shang,

333
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:08,300
you've got some nerve!

334
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:11,540
No one's ever dared treat me this way.

335
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:15,140
I'm sorry.

336
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:17,500
I was already regretting it yesterday.

337
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:18,980
Your regret means nothing to me!

338
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:24,620
For the sake of this box of rouge,

339
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:27,780
I'll forgive you.

340
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:29,140
And what's more,

341
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:30,940
I'll grant your wish.

342
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:37,020
Chunhua.

343
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:39,140
Tell them to pack and prepare to leave.

344
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:42,700
Now I understand

345
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:46,380
why you want to leave Lingnan.

346
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:50,620
Father...

347
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:56,820
You were right that night.

348
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:00,220
I've hidden away here for years,

349
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:03,020
as good as dead.

350
00:24:04,540 --> 00:24:06,540
Dalang is simple-minded now

351
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:09,340
and is destined to live out his days
in the countryside.

352
00:24:11,260 --> 00:24:12,380
As your father,

353
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:16,100
I've failed you both.

354
00:24:18,860 --> 00:24:20,100
And Xiaozhou has had a hard time, too.

355
00:24:30,180 --> 00:24:30,580
Father,

356
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:32,580
actually, I envy my elder brother.

357
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:35,180
He told me

358
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:38,020
when the rice ears emerge,

359
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:39,260
he's happy.

360
00:24:40,420 --> 00:24:41,380
Happy when it rains

361
00:24:41,740 --> 00:24:42,300
and cools down.

362
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:45,020
Happy when Xiaozhou

363
00:24:46,020 --> 00:24:46,740
cooks something good.

364
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:49,060
Once,

365
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:51,580
he caught a beautiful dragonfly for me

366
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:54,100
and was happy for ages.

367
00:24:56,580 --> 00:24:57,900
To eat one's fill and roam freely.

368
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:01,660
That's the ideal
the sage Zhuangzi pursued all his life.

369
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:03,540
My elder brother has achieved it.

370
00:25:09,940 --> 00:25:10,740
I'm far from his equal.

371
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:13,460
With desires in my heart,

372
00:25:14,500 --> 00:25:15,460
I only torment myself.

373
00:25:25,220 --> 00:25:26,740
With the talent to achieve great things,

374
00:25:27,980 --> 00:25:29,700
how can you not aspire
to soar like a roc?

375
00:25:30,740 --> 00:25:31,700
Sheng'an may be far away,

376
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:33,460
but you can make it there.

377
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:38,460
You've thought this through
better than I have.

378
00:25:40,060 --> 00:25:40,900
Whatever you want to do,

379
00:25:43,140 --> 00:25:43,820
go ahead and do it.

380
00:26:03,020 --> 00:26:03,580
(I wonder)

381
00:26:05,020 --> 00:26:06,220
(where she is now.)

382
00:26:13,060 --> 00:26:14,580
So much for Lingxi's fine wine.

383
00:26:14,860 --> 00:26:15,580
It's nothing special.

384
00:26:23,420 --> 00:26:24,420
My lady, headache again?

385
00:26:25,180 --> 00:26:26,300
Did you sleep poorly last night?

386
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:41,060
What's wrong?

387
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:42,580
My lady, don't get out.

388
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:44,260
There seems to be a wild beast nearby.

389
00:26:58,460 --> 00:26:58,940
(Watch out!)

390
00:26:58,940 --> 00:26:59,460
(Watch out!)

391
00:26:59,460 --> 00:27:00,220
(Hold the carriage steady!)

392
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:00,700
(Back away!)

393
00:27:00,700 --> 00:27:01,180
(Watch out!)

394
00:27:02,820 --> 00:27:03,300
Your Highness!

395
00:27:03,340 --> 00:27:03,980
Your Highness!

396
00:28:23,780 --> 00:28:24,220
I'm fine.

397
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:27,900
It's nothing.

398
00:28:28,300 --> 00:28:29,220
When the tutor asks about it later,

399
00:28:29,420 --> 00:28:29,820
just say

400
00:28:30,260 --> 00:28:31,420
his cat broke it.

401
00:28:33,660 --> 00:28:34,340
(Diligent Study, Steadfast Practice)
What happened just now?

402
00:28:35,820 --> 00:28:36,340
Nothing.

403
00:28:36,860 --> 00:28:38,380
My heart suddenly skipped a beat.

404
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:40,220
Perhaps I didn't sleep well last night.

405
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:44,460
(Learning without thought is labor lost;
thought without learning is perilous.)

406
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:44,900
Shang,

407
00:28:45,700 --> 00:28:46,460
am I seeing things?

408
00:28:47,060 --> 00:28:48,820
If I didn't know you were a bachelor,

409
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:52,100
I'd think
you'd been mooning over a girl all day.

410
00:28:54,460 --> 00:28:55,580
The results are posted tomorrow.

411
00:28:55,980 --> 00:28:56,660
At a time like this,

412
00:28:57,060 --> 00:28:58,300
you still have time to tease me.

413
00:28:59,140 --> 00:28:59,900
It's only the local qualifying exam.

414
00:29:00,300 --> 00:29:01,100
It's not worth worrying over.

415
00:29:02,180 --> 00:29:03,340
My name will definitely

416
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:05,100
be on the list.

417
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:07,820
That's true.

418
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:09,180
When it comes

419
00:29:09,740 --> 00:29:11,020
to poetry and rhapsody, classical
interpretation, or policy essays,

420
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:13,340
no one can match you.

421
00:29:13,780 --> 00:29:15,060
Even if Lingnan selects
only one candidate,

422
00:29:15,660 --> 00:29:16,340
it'll surely be you.

423
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:19,180
Shang,

424
00:29:19,940 --> 00:29:20,300
you're wrong.

425
00:29:20,780 --> 00:29:21,940
(Diligent Study, Steadfast Practice)
The people in these schools

426
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:23,700
are all mediocre nobodies.

427
00:29:24,020 --> 00:29:25,340
They're not even worth comparing to me.

428
00:29:25,820 --> 00:29:27,100
But in classical interpretation
and policy essays,

429
00:29:27,620 --> 00:29:28,580
isn't there someone right here

430
00:29:29,300 --> 00:29:30,380
who can match me?

431
00:29:30,860 --> 00:29:32,300
If only you had
household registration...

432
00:29:36,460 --> 00:29:37,300
Well, Wenji,

433
00:29:38,060 --> 00:29:39,260
you know every subject there is

434
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:40,100
except common decency.

435
00:29:40,700 --> 00:29:41,380
A few words in,

436
00:29:42,060 --> 00:29:43,180
and you're already reopening
my old wounds.

437
00:29:47,940 --> 00:29:48,660
There'll be a way.

438
00:29:53,700 --> 00:29:54,380
That's right.

439
00:29:56,180 --> 00:29:57,260
There'll be a way.

440
00:30:06,020 --> 00:30:06,420
(Your Highness?)

441
00:30:06,620 --> 00:30:07,500
(Find the Princess!)

442
00:30:07,700 --> 00:30:08,260
(Your Highness?)

443
00:30:09,260 --> 00:30:09,780
(Your Highness?)

444
00:30:17,260 --> 00:30:18,020
(Your Highness?)

445
00:30:18,020 --> 00:30:18,540
(Come on, pull!)

446
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:19,140
(Come on!)

447
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:20,580
(Over here! Two more people!)

448
00:30:20,580 --> 00:30:21,700
- (Your Highness?)
- (Your Highness?)

449
00:30:21,700 --> 00:30:22,220
(Hurry!)

450
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:22,820
(Your Highness?)

451
00:30:22,820 --> 00:30:23,540
My lady said...

452
00:30:23,620 --> 00:30:23,980
(Your Highness?)

453
00:30:23,980 --> 00:30:25,220
we mustn't call her that out here.

454
00:30:25,220 --> 00:30:25,780
(Your Highness?)

455
00:30:26,260 --> 00:30:26,940
(To the left! Hurry!)

456
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:27,900
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

457
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:29,900
- (My lady?)
- (Where are you?)

458
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:30,460
(My lady?)

459
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:31,460
(My lady?)

460
00:30:31,460 --> 00:30:31,980
(Search over there!)

461
00:30:31,980 --> 00:30:32,540
Fang Tong,

462
00:30:33,460 --> 00:30:34,460
what do we do?

463
00:30:35,020 --> 00:30:35,340
No.

464
00:30:35,340 --> 00:30:36,020
(Come on!)

465
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:36,940
We must notify the authorities

466
00:30:37,420 --> 00:30:38,260
and get more people to help search.

467
00:30:38,780 --> 00:30:39,700
But my lady forbade it.

468
00:30:40,100 --> 00:30:40,420
(Careful!)

469
00:30:40,420 --> 00:30:41,300
As long as we find her,

470
00:30:41,660 --> 00:30:42,620
I'll accept any punishment.

471
00:30:42,860 --> 00:30:43,300
(Everyone, lend a hand!)

472
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:44,580
We must find her before dark.

473
00:30:45,060 --> 00:30:46,300
Once night falls in these wild woods,

474
00:30:46,700 --> 00:30:47,500
there'll be beasts everywhere.

475
00:30:49,140 --> 00:30:49,700
(Come on, give it here!)

476
00:30:49,900 --> 00:30:51,020
You two, search over there!

477
00:30:51,020 --> 00:30:51,300
(Careful!)

478
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:51,820
- Yes!
- Yes!

479
00:32:12,940 --> 00:32:13,780
(The carriage fell in.)

480
00:32:14,420 --> 00:32:15,380
(It would've drifted downstream.)

481
00:32:16,620 --> 00:32:17,620
(If I head upstream,)

482
00:32:18,700 --> 00:32:20,220
(I might find where it fell in.)

483
00:33:07,900 --> 00:33:09,260
(My lady?)

484
00:33:10,020 --> 00:33:11,060
(My lady?)

485
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:11,580
(Search carefully!)

486
00:33:12,020 --> 00:33:12,820
(My lady?)

487
00:33:14,020 --> 00:33:14,380
Sir,

488
00:33:14,820 --> 00:33:15,460
what happened?

489
00:33:15,540 --> 00:33:16,020
We're looking for the lady.

490
00:33:16,020 --> 00:33:17,620
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

491
00:33:17,700 --> 00:33:18,980
(My lady?)

492
00:33:18,980 --> 00:33:20,100
(Why don't we check over there?)

493
00:33:20,340 --> 00:33:21,100
- (All right.)
- (No sign of her here!)

494
00:33:21,380 --> 00:33:22,300
My lady?

495
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:23,380
(My lady?)

496
00:33:23,420 --> 00:33:24,060
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

497
00:33:24,060 --> 00:33:26,460
- My lady, where are you?
- (My lady?)

498
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:27,660
(Hurry! Search carefully!)

499
00:33:27,980 --> 00:33:28,780
(My lady?)

500
00:33:28,980 --> 00:33:29,620
Miss Chunhua!

501
00:33:29,620 --> 00:33:31,100
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

502
00:33:31,100 --> 00:33:31,500
What happened?

503
00:33:32,540 --> 00:33:33,260
Where's your lady?

504
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:34,100
Yan Shang...

505
00:33:34,820 --> 00:33:35,820
(My lady?)

506
00:33:35,980 --> 00:33:37,940
My lady is missing.

507
00:33:37,940 --> 00:33:38,380
Missing?

508
00:33:39,140 --> 00:33:39,700
How did she go missing?

509
00:33:39,820 --> 00:33:41,180
A tiger spooked the horses

510
00:33:41,620 --> 00:33:44,460
and the carriage overturned
and fell into the river...

511
00:33:45,580 --> 00:33:46,460
My lady?

512
00:33:47,100 --> 00:33:47,900
When did this happen?

513
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:51,060
It's been most of the day.

514
00:33:52,980 --> 00:33:53,940
(My lady?)

515
00:33:54,340 --> 00:33:55,220
(Search thoroughly!)

516
00:33:55,220 --> 00:33:55,940
(Check over there!)

517
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:56,540
(No slacking off!)

518
00:33:57,020 --> 00:33:57,780
(My lady?)

519
00:33:57,780 --> 00:33:58,100
Sir,

520
00:33:58,700 --> 00:33:59,220
this isn't the way to search.

521
00:33:59,220 --> 00:34:00,380
You again?

522
00:34:00,820 --> 00:34:01,540
It's been hours since the accident.

523
00:34:01,660 --> 00:34:02,460
She's probably injured.

524
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:03,820
Her voice must be weak.

525
00:34:04,380 --> 00:34:05,460
With everyone shouting at once,

526
00:34:05,820 --> 00:34:07,140
we wouldn't hear her
even if she cried for help.

527
00:34:07,620 --> 00:34:07,980
Besides,

528
00:34:08,500 --> 00:34:09,340
night is falling.

529
00:34:09,780 --> 00:34:10,540
She has no torch.

530
00:34:10,780 --> 00:34:11,780
All this torchlight in our eyes...

531
00:34:11,780 --> 00:34:12,500
My lady?

532
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:14,140
... will make it even harder
to see through the woods.

533
00:34:14,380 --> 00:34:16,580
Are you telling me how to do my job?

534
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:19,380
Right now, finding her
is our top priority.

535
00:34:19,380 --> 00:34:19,940
Then move aside!

536
00:34:20,300 --> 00:34:21,260
Don't interfere with official business!

537
00:34:21,900 --> 00:34:23,140
Walk through the woods without a torch?

538
00:34:23,140 --> 00:34:23,940
Do I have a death wish?

539
00:34:24,380 --> 00:34:25,540
Aren't you carrying one yourself?

540
00:34:26,100 --> 00:34:27,020
And you're lecturing me?

541
00:34:27,740 --> 00:34:28,940
Search carefully!

542
00:34:29,540 --> 00:34:30,820
The sooner we find her,

543
00:34:31,260 --> 00:34:32,740
the sooner we can go home!

544
00:34:32,740 --> 00:34:33,260
(Don't die.)

545
00:34:33,460 --> 00:34:33,780
(Yes!)

546
00:34:33,860 --> 00:34:34,460
(My lady?)

547
00:34:38,180 --> 00:34:39,340
(No slacking! Search carefully!)

548
00:34:39,340 --> 00:34:40,100
(My lady?)

549
00:34:40,220 --> 00:34:41,140
(My lady?)

550
00:34:41,780 --> 00:34:42,060
(Hurry!)

551
00:34:47,660 --> 00:34:49,420
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

552
00:37:43,620 --> 00:37:44,820
Mother...

553
00:37:46,580 --> 00:37:52,700
♪A daughter ventures forth,
in the name her father gave♪

554
00:37:53,100 --> 00:37:59,100
♪Into savage lands, to tame tigers
and slay wolves♪

555
00:37:59,220 --> 00:37:59,940
Mother...

556
00:38:02,140 --> 00:38:03,060
Mother...

557
00:38:03,060 --> 00:38:06,820
♪The fate is sealed,
a destiny bestowed by Heaven♪

558
00:38:07,540 --> 00:38:11,080
♪When did you decide to defy it,
to change it?♪

559
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:14,620
♪When did you decide to defy it,
to change it?♪

560
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:18,740
♪Defy its might,
and the submission it demands♪

561
00:38:18,740 --> 00:38:22,300
♪Defy its might,
and the submission it demands♪

562
00:38:22,740 --> 00:38:23,740
(Wanyao, don't cry.)

563
00:38:23,740 --> 00:38:27,700
♪Defy its scorn,
stain the sky with blood♪

564
00:38:27,700 --> 00:38:28,860
(My Wanyao,)

565
00:38:30,340 --> 00:38:31,540
(you're the bravest, aren't you?)

566
00:38:31,540 --> 00:38:34,060
♪We weren't born for sacrifice.
Love isn't meant for silent suffering♪

567
00:38:34,180 --> 00:38:35,620
♪Nor wed for the sake of any kingdom♪

568
00:38:35,620 --> 00:38:35,940
(Come on.)

569
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:38,860
♪Cold as a blade,
yet peerless as a bloom♪

570
00:38:38,860 --> 00:38:39,620
(Have a piece of candy.)

571
00:38:40,820 --> 00:38:44,180
♪Who dares make me bow
down in the dust?♪

572
00:38:44,300 --> 00:38:48,420
♪With sacrificed innocence
and a soul snowbound♪

573
00:38:48,700 --> 00:38:51,060
♪If the road is blocked,
I'll fight my way through♪

574
00:38:51,260 --> 00:38:54,260
♪Cut down the crowd,
strike down the proud gods♪

575
00:38:54,460 --> 00:38:57,500
♪Break through Hell's gates♪

576
00:38:58,220 --> 00:39:02,260
♪If I could meet my former self again♪

577
00:39:02,780 --> 00:39:05,580
♪Don't be afraid,
I'll become a demon for you♪

578
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:11,820
♪Through fire, I'll turn the dark towers
bright as day for you♪

579
00:39:12,500 --> 00:39:16,260
♪Though this world is hard to cross,
I'll lead you through♪

580
00:39:16,460 --> 00:39:19,460
♪I dare face the unknown,
with my sword in hand♪

581
00:39:19,740 --> 00:39:24,500
♪I'll guard my princess,
and keep her tears at bay♪

582
00:39:36,900 --> 00:39:42,420
My lady? My lady?

583
00:39:42,420 --> 00:39:45,220
My lady? My lady?

584
00:39:45,220 --> 00:39:46,460
(We've wasted too much time here.)

585
00:39:46,460 --> 00:39:47,380
(Everyone, search carefully!)

586
00:39:47,620 --> 00:39:48,380
(My lady?)

587
00:39:48,380 --> 00:39:49,340
- (Search carefully!)
- (My lady?)

588
00:39:49,780 --> 00:39:50,580
(My lady?)

589
00:39:50,820 --> 00:39:51,980
(A few of you,
come check over there with me!)

590
00:39:51,980 --> 00:39:53,420
(My lady? My lady?)

591
00:39:56,700 --> 00:39:57,580
(My lady?)

592
00:40:30,700 --> 00:40:31,420
(My lady?)

593
00:40:33,620 --> 00:40:34,860
- (My lady?)
- (Can you hear us?)

594
00:40:34,860 --> 00:40:35,780
(Have you searched over there?)

595
00:40:35,900 --> 00:40:36,940
(My lady?)

596
00:40:38,020 --> 00:40:38,900
(Check over there!)

597
00:40:43,660 --> 00:40:44,540
(My lady?)

598
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:46,780
(My lady?)

599
00:40:46,780 --> 00:40:47,220
(No sign of her here!)

600
00:40:49,620 --> 00:40:50,700
(My lady?)

601
00:40:51,180 --> 00:40:51,980
I'm here!

602
00:40:51,980 --> 00:40:54,860
My lady? My lady?

603
00:40:54,860 --> 00:40:55,980
I'm here!

604
00:40:56,820 --> 00:40:57,420
(What about over there?)

605
00:40:57,900 --> 00:40:58,740
(No sign of her here!)

606
00:40:58,820 --> 00:40:59,460
(We've searched over there!)

607
00:40:59,460 --> 00:41:00,100
I'm here!

608
00:41:00,180 --> 00:41:00,860
(Can you hear us?)

609
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:01,700
I'm here!

610
00:41:03,380 --> 00:41:04,500
- (My lady?)
- I'm here...

611
00:41:04,860 --> 00:41:06,260
- (My lady?)
- (My lady?)

612
00:41:06,820 --> 00:41:07,900
I'm here...

613
00:41:09,180 --> 00:41:10,020
I'm here...

614
00:41:12,060 --> 00:41:13,100
(My lady?)

615
00:41:13,740 --> 00:41:14,980
I'm here!

616
00:42:07,180 --> 00:42:11,780
(Next Episode Preview)

617
00:42:12,060 --> 00:42:12,660
I want to take a bath.

618
00:42:13,700 --> 00:42:14,420
Carry me over.

619
00:42:18,020 --> 00:42:18,700
If you leave,

620
00:42:19,340 --> 00:42:20,620
who'll wait on me while I bathe?

621
00:42:22,380 --> 00:42:22,860
Bath powder.

622
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:31,853
♪Be the ferry
where you wait for the sun♪

623
00:42:34,538 --> 00:42:39,454
♪Be the blue silk
that catches your tears♪

624
00:42:41,648 --> 00:42:47,493
♪Be the sleeve we held,
worn by dust and years♪

625
00:42:47,993 --> 00:42:53,219
♪Let's conspire to grow old together♪

626
00:42:55,988 --> 00:43:00,779
♪Let me be a captive beast
bound by the same lock as you♪

627
00:43:01,615 --> 00:43:07,694
♪Through trails of mud and blood;
let grief drown in your eyes♪

628
00:43:09,495 --> 00:43:12,645
♪Soar with the wind;
plunge into hellfire as one♪

629
00:43:12,645 --> 00:43:14,293
♪Burning bright as a song♪

630
00:43:14,345 --> 00:43:18,069
♪See how roses and green bamboo enchant♪

631
00:43:18,447 --> 00:43:23,113
♪Be the vow I make with all my heart♪

632
00:43:23,732 --> 00:43:27,773
♪If we say forever,
then forever it shall be♪

633
00:43:28,264 --> 00:43:30,379
♪Not a single hour less♪

634
00:43:30,419 --> 00:43:37,365
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

635
00:43:38,128 --> 00:43:41,581
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

636
00:43:41,761 --> 00:43:44,906
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

637
00:43:45,345 --> 00:43:51,982
♪If we can stay, let's return
to the village of our first meeting♪

638
00:43:52,379 --> 00:43:56,893
♪May time be free of fear and pain;
boats rock, lights fade, seasons turn♪

639
00:43:56,931 --> 00:43:59,400
♪You're the only one I need♪

640
00:43:59,604 --> 00:44:06,491
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

641
00:44:06,803 --> 00:44:10,074
♪Be mine in this world;
be mine in this life♪

642
00:44:10,379 --> 00:44:13,552
♪My last untouched innocence♪

643
00:44:13,876 --> 00:44:17,302
♪If only we could return
to the village where we first met♪

644
00:44:17,535 --> 00:44:20,760
♪Stay by me; help me forget
the frozen dream of last night♪

645
00:44:21,091 --> 00:44:27,887
♪Fireflies glow, flowers kiss our lips;
just us, through dawn and dusk♪

646
00:44:28,256 --> 00:44:32,822
♪May time be free of fear and pain;
boats rock, lights fade, seasons turn♪

647
00:44:32,869 --> 00:44:35,207
♪You're the only one I need♪

648
00:44:35,438 --> 00:44:42,273
♪By your side, through joy and pain,
is that eternity?♪

649
00:44:42,622 --> 00:44:44,240
♪Till fireworks flood the town♪

650
00:44:44,370 --> 00:44:46,166
♪Till the lake is still and clear♪

651
00:44:46,523 --> 00:44:49,540
♪You're the only one I need♪

652
00:44:49,580 --> 00:44:50,907
(No animals were harmed
or mistreated in production.)
